{
  "sn55.21:0.1": "Linked Discourses 55.21 ",
  "sn55.21:0.2": "3. About Sarakāni ",
  "sn55.21:0.3": "With Mahānāma (1st) ",
  "sn55.21:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn55.21:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Sakyans, near Kapilavatthu in the Banyan Tree Monastery. ",
  "sn55.21:1.3": "Then Mahānāma the Sakyan went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "sn55.21:1.4": "“Sir, this Kapilavatthu is successful and prosperous, populous and full of people, with cramped cul-de-sacs. ",
  "sn55.21:1.5": "In the late afternoon, after paying homage to the Buddha or an esteemed mendicant, I enter Kapilavatthu. ",
  "sn55.21:1.6": "I encounter a stray elephant, ",
  "sn55.21:1.7": "horse, ",
  "sn55.21:1.8": "chariot, ",
  "sn55.21:1.9": "cart, ",
  "sn55.21:1.10": "or person. ",
  "sn55.21:1.11": "At that time I lose mindfulness regarding the Buddha, the teaching, and the Saṅgha. ",
  "sn55.21:1.12": "I think: ",
  "sn55.21:1.13": "‘If I were to die at this time, where would I be reborn in my next life?’” ",
  "sn55.21:2.1": "“Do not fear, Mahānāma, do not fear! ",
  "sn55.21:2.2": "Your death will not be a bad one; your passing will not be a bad one. ",
  "sn55.21:2.3": "Take someone whose mind has for a long time been imbued with faith, ethics, learning, generosity, and wisdom. Their body is formed, made up of the four principal states, produced by mother and father, built up from rice and porridge, liable to impermanence, to wearing away and e